      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 58-year-old man developed ventricular fibrillation and a large anterior infarction one hour after a negative exercise test. Coronary angiography post-infarction suggested the presence of a \"complicated\" lesion, raising the possibility that the infarction resulted from sudden occlusion of a previously nonsignificant lesion."},
